{
  "2-2": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset: ONE complete 3:2 overhead slightly oblique Indonesian RPG outdoor map, native output 1536x1024, full-frame. Primary request: upscale and reconstruct fine native raster detail, matching the crisp visual quality of references, never simply magnify soft pixels. Image 1 is the ONLY edit target. Image 2 is map 2-1, mandatory same-world palette, foliage texture, beige square paving, gray stone walls, warm orange lamplight and density of crisp detailed leaves reference. Image 3 is map 1-1, mandatory native detail/sharpness reference only, not layout. Further images are adjacent maps for edge continuity only. Preserve target composition and exact normalized positions, sizes, entrances, walkways, roofs, stairs, obstacles and playable clearings. Do not shift, rotate, zoom, crop or add objects. Enhance individual leaves, flower petals, roof tiles, grout, windows and tiny textures with crisp clean hand-painted RPG detail at final native resolution. Maintain consistent vivid tropical green/teal vegetation, warm peach beige paving, subtle cool gray stone and orange lamps, balanced exposure matching image 2; keep nighttime stage illumination where present without a different color cast on ground/foliage. Keep all existing roads and stairs open at original locations. At facing borders preserve the neighboring ground geometry, paving line spacing, grass hue and road widths, and smoothly continue shared vegetation; no seam stripe, new boundary wall or blocking tree. No added people, monsters, interface, watermark, nameplate, collage, atlas, or reference map included. Output ONLY the whole edited image 1, at least 1536x1024 with meaningful crisp reconstructed detail.\nTarget: Kota Beton with large white oval stadium, red-orange front motif, clinic lower right and canteen lower left. Image 4 (2-3 Festival) lies directly WEST of the target: target LEFT edge matches image 4 RIGHT. Image 5 (2-4 Pasar Malam) lies directly SOUTH: target BOTTOM matches image 5 TOP. Keep stadium silhouette and all paths/doors exactly positioned. Target is northeast tile in chapter 2.",
  "2-3": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset: ONE complete 3:2 overhead slightly oblique Indonesian RPG outdoor map, native output 1536x1024, full-frame. Primary request: upscale and reconstruct fine native raster detail, matching the crisp visual quality of references, never simply magnify soft pixels. Image 1 is the ONLY edit target. Image 2 is map 2-1, mandatory same-world palette, foliage texture, beige square paving, gray stone walls, warm orange lamplight and density of crisp detailed leaves reference. Image 3 is map 1-1, mandatory native detail/sharpness reference only, not layout. Further images are adjacent maps for edge continuity only. Preserve target composition and exact normalized positions, sizes, entrances, walkways, roofs, stairs, obstacles and playable clearings. Do not shift, rotate, zoom, crop or add objects. Enhance individual leaves, flower petals, roof tiles, grout, windows and tiny textures with crisp clean hand-painted RPG detail at final native resolution. Maintain consistent vivid tropical green/teal vegetation, warm peach beige paving, subtle cool gray stone and orange lamps, balanced exposure matching image 2; keep nighttime stage illumination where present without a different color cast on ground/foliage. Keep all existing roads and stairs open at original locations. At facing borders preserve the neighboring ground geometry, paving line spacing, grass hue and road widths, and smoothly continue shared vegetation; no seam stripe, new boundary wall or blocking tree. No added people, monsters, interface, watermark, nameplate, collage, atlas, or reference map included. Output ONLY the whole edited image 1, at least 1536x1024 with meaningful crisp reconstructed detail.\nTarget: Festival Arus, concert stage top center, central festival plaza, stalls and lower center stair/exit. Image 4 (2-2 Kota Beton) lies directly EAST: target RIGHT edge matches image 4 LEFT. Image 2 (2-1 Terminal) lies directly SOUTH: target BOTTOM edge matches image 2 TOP, including central paving approach. Preserve stage purple/magenta lights, but let shared outdoor vegetation and paving use image 2 colors and brightness. Target is northwest tile in chapter 2.",
  "2-4": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset: ONE complete 3:2 overhead slightly oblique Indonesian RPG outdoor map, native output 1536x1024, full-frame. Primary request: upscale and reconstruct fine native raster detail, matching the crisp visual quality of references, never simply magnify soft pixels. Image 1 is the ONLY edit target. Image 2 is map 2-1, mandatory same-world palette, foliage texture, beige square paving, gray stone walls, warm orange lamplight and density of crisp detailed leaves reference. Image 3 is map 1-1, mandatory native detail/sharpness reference only, not layout. Further images are adjacent maps for edge continuity only. Preserve target composition and exact normalized positions, sizes, entrances, walkways, roofs, stairs, obstacles and playable clearings. Do not shift, rotate, zoom, crop or add objects. Enhance individual leaves, flower petals, roof tiles, grout, windows and tiny textures with crisp clean hand-painted RPG detail at final native resolution. Maintain consistent vivid tropical green/teal vegetation, warm peach beige paving, subtle cool gray stone and orange lamps, balanced exposure matching image 2; keep nighttime stage illumination where present without a different color cast on ground/foliage. Keep all existing roads and stairs open at original locations. At facing borders preserve the neighboring ground geometry, paving line spacing, grass hue and road widths, and smoothly continue shared vegetation; no seam stripe, new boundary wall or blocking tree. No added people, monsters, interface, watermark, nameplate, collage, atlas, or reference map included. Output ONLY the whole edited image 1, at least 1536x1024 with meaningful crisp reconstructed detail.\nTarget: Pasar Malam market with traditional wooden music pavilion centered, stalls and broad plaza. Image 4 (2-2 Kota Beton) lies directly NORTH: target TOP edge matches image 4 BOTTOM. Image 2 (2-1 Terminal) lies directly WEST: target LEFT edge matches image 2 RIGHT. Improve the soft existing leaves and pavilion/roof detail, retaining warm lantern evening appearance. Target is southeast tile in chapter 2."
}

